# FALSE-FAIL GUARD (Lesson: validity checks need false-fail suites).
# Initialization seeds S(N) = {N, top} for every node, so bottom IN S(bottom) holds
# BY CONSTRUCTION the moment owl:Nothing appears -- which any disjointness axiom
# guarantees. owl:Nothing MUST be excluded from `unsatisfiable` by name, or every
# real ontology reports itself incoherent and `howl validate` exits 1 universally.
# Expect: COHERENT, unsatisfiable EMPTY.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:C owl:disjointWith :D .
